# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The human essay corpus is other people's writing under licences that do not
# permit redistribution. Rebuild it with scripts/fetch_corpus.py; provenance and
# per-document SHA-256 hashes live in data/manifest/ and
# src/palimpsest/data/sources.py so a rebuild can be proved identical.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/raw/
data/features/

# Derived corpora that EMBED that human text are equally not ours to redistribute.
# Both are reproducible: build_real_hybrids.py needs data/raw/, and the hand-written
# hybrids are spliced onto Liang essays.
data/generated/real_hybrid_essays.jsonl
data/generated/hybrid_essays.jsonl

# data/generated/machine_essays.jsonl IS committed -- we wrote those essays, so they
# are ours to publish, and they are the adversarial set the evaluation reports on.

# The same reasoning covers the modern-generator corpus: our prompts, model output, no human
# writing embedded, so modern_train/holdout/unseen.jsonl are committed and a reader can check
# that the split really does keep one model out of training. `parts/` is the per-model
# scratch the generator writes before the split merges it, and committing it would put every
# essay in the repository twice.
data/generated/parts/

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.DS_Store

# Fetched by scripts/fetch_external.py, licence undeclared on the mirror -> not
# redistributed here. See docs/02-dataset.md.
data/raw/daigt.jsonl

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The remote observer's response cache. This is NOT just numbers: each entry stores
# every token with its character offsets, so the ORIGINAL ESSAY can be reconstructed
# from it verbatim -- including the ELLIPSE, PERSUADE and TOEFL essays written by real
# students. Committing it would republish, through the back door, exactly the corpus
# `data/raw/` above is excluded to protect. It is also ~240 MB and is rebuilt for free
# by re-running the scorer.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/cache/

# Snapshots taken before a retrain so the two could be compared. Scratch, not results.
artifacts/_before/

# Safety nets: no credential or dependency tree belongs in this repository.
.env
*.env
!observer-worker/.env.example
node_modules/
